# Board 1.62. Whoever can run Arbor today builds it, and docks a terminal first. Terminal sizes its window in whole character
# cells (7 x 15 points beside a margin of 2 x 4, measured) and takes the cells NEAREST to what it is asked for, which half the time
# is more: offered 852 points it takes 859. It used to be talked down a line every time its slot came back: a line up and a line
# down at every return of the view.
quiet
display-size 1440x900 24
open Terminal 585x394 cell 7x15 margin 2x4
open Notes

# The first meeting. Nobody can know a cell before an app has shown it: it is talked down once, where it stands.
dock 101 left
expect docked 101
expect at 101 12 36
expect size 101 702x844

# From then on it is asked for the whole cells that fit its slot, and takes them as they are: one move.
dock 102 right
expect moved-once
expect at 101 12 36
expect size 101 464x844

# Away and back, as often as one likes: the same frame, by one move.
zoom 102
home
expect moved-once
expect at 101 12 36
expect size 101 464x844
zoom 102
home
expect moved-once
expect size 101 464x844
zoom 102
home
expect moved-once
expect size 101 464x844

# A layout of the same slot asks it for nothing.
show-all
expect still

# What is left of the slot, less than a cell, is at the bottom, where the app leaves it. Nobody pays for it: Notes has its own
# slot, and the gap between the two is where it was.
expect left-of 101 102
expect at 102 964 36
expect size 102 464x852

# A gap moved by less than a cell: the terminal has nothing to do. By more: one move.
resize 101 right 3
expect still 101
resize 101 right 10
expect moved-once
expect at 101 12 36
expect size 101 478x844

# Zoomed in on: another slot, and what is asked for is worked out from that one. And back.
zoom 101
expect moved-once
expect at 101 12 36
expect size 101 1416x844
home
expect at 101 12 36
expect size 101 478x844

# A terminal that takes the cells that fit, never more, is asked for the slot itself, and stays in its corner as well.
open iTerm 600x400 cell 8x17 down margin 2x30
dock 103 beside 101 bottom
expect at 101 12 36
expect size 101 478x409
expect at 103 12 468
expect size 103 474x404
zoom 102
home
expect moved-once
expect at 103 12 468
expect size 103 474x404
expect size 101 478x409

# Quit, which gives every window its own size back, and start again. Arbor knows nothing of cells any more, and finds the same frames.
relaunch
expect size 101 478x409
expect size 103 474x404

# A larger font: other cells, so what was learnt of the old ones is worth nothing. It is learnt anew, and holds again.
cell 101 8x17 margin 2x4
relayout
expect docked 101
expect at 101 12 36
zoom 102
home
expect moved-once
expect at 101 12 36
